Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 03:17:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] desktop: cap the decoded-image cache, and BB_DIAG startup
 and frame diagnostics

Flutter keeps up to 100 MB (1000 images) of decoded bitmaps; most of the RSS
growth while scrolling the chat list came from it. Cap it at 48 MB / 300 images
(BB_IMAGE_CACHE_MB overrides). BB_DIAG=1 prints startup marks (dart main,
database, services, first frame, splash closed, UI ready), the display the engine
sees, and every five seconds the frame count with build and raster times, which
tells an idle app that still draws from a scroll that cannot reach 120 fps.
